      "term": "Mot",
      "matchText": "Mot",
      "wikiSlug": "",
      "type": "concept",
      "definition": "The Canaanite-Phoenician god of death and the underworld. In the Baal Cycle he is Baal's enemy, killing and devouring the storm god each year before Baal returns to life — a death-and-rebirth myth that mirrored the agricultural seasons."
    },
    {
      "term": "Yam",
      "matchText": "Yam",
      "wikiSlug": "",
      "type": "concept",
      "definition": "The Canaanite-Phoenician god of the sea, embodying the chaotic ocean. In the Baal Cycle the storm god Baal must defeat Yam to take his place among the gods — a combat myth echoed across the ancient Near East."
    },
