    {
      "term": "Temple of Melqart",
      "matchText": "Temple of Melqart",
      "type": "place",
      "definition": "The chief temple of Tyre, dedicated to the city's patron god Melqart. It was the religious heart of the Tyrian world and the spiritual center of a network of daughter-temples in Phoenician colonies (Carthage's Tophet and the temple at Gades among them). Alexander's stated reason for entering Tyre was to sacrifice here; the Tyrians' refusal to admit him triggered the siege."
